             Digital Delivers Powerful New Windows Based
               PC Client Server Solutions and Software


          New Products Secure Digital as the Logical Choice
            for Windows NT Products Across the Enterprise


MAYNARD, Mass., September 9, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced powerful new solutions within its desktop PC, 
notebook computer and PC server product lines that are optimized for 
the Windows NT(R) operating system.  Today's announcements 
complement Digital's broad range of computing solutions, worldwide 
service and support, enterprise software enhancements and strategic
alliance with Microsoft -- establishing Digital as the logical 
choice for customers who require Windows NT-based computing 
solutions.  Included in today's announcements are:  

     o  Venturis GL Desktop PCs:  A powerful Pentium Pro addition to 
        Digital's recently introduced Venturis FX Pentium family of 
        value line desktops, rounding out the company's Venturis 
        line with new levels of price-performance -- Optimized for 
        Windows NT Workstation.

     o  Celebris FX and Celebris GL Desktop PCs:  A complete new 
        line of "enterprise-ready" Pentium and Pentium Pro Celebris 
        desktop PCs, feature-rich and highly integrated solutions 
        that bring the power of the enterprise to the desktop -- 
        Optimized for Windows NT Workstation.

     o  HiNote Ultra II with Windows NT 4.0:  The industry's only 
        notebook computer with Windows NT 4.0 pre-loaded and pre-
     	configured, including unprecedented power management and 
        plug-and-play-like features developed exclusively by
     	Digital -- Optimized for Windows NT Workstation.

     o  ClientWORKS 2.3:  The latest version of Digital's popular 
        client-management software -- included with all Digital 
        desktop, notebook and personal workstation platforms -- now 
        features new system management capabilities for reporting 
        asset management information to the company's network 
        administration and server software, Digital ServerWORKS -- 
        Optimized for Windows NT Workstation.

     o  ServerWORKS Manager 2.0:  Easy to use, standards-based 
        management software that supports multiple server operating 
        environments and simplifies server and network 
        administration, reducing total cost of ownership.  New 
        features include remote paging, management of Windows NT 
        clustered servers, an intelligent toolbar and integration 
        with Digital's DMI-based ClientWORKS software -- Optimized 
        for Windows NT Server.

     o  Digital Clusters for Windows NT Server 1.0a:  The industry's 
        most cost-effective software for high availability under 
        Windows NT Server 4.0, including failover support for 
        Microsoft SQL Server, Oracle Workgroup Server and Windows NT 
        File Services.  New features include simplified installation 
        and management with ServerWORKS Quick Launch, ServerWORKS 
        Manager and a Prioris Server Cluster Kit -- Optimized for 
        Windows NT Server.

     o  Digital Personal Workstations:  Plans to extend Digital's 
        industry-leading Personal Workstation line with a 
        next-generation family of high-performance workstations 
        based on Intel's Pentium Pro microprocessor -- Optimized for
     	Windows NT Workstation.

     "Today marks an important milestone for Digital as we execute 
on our strategy to drive Windows NT computing solutions across the 
enterprise," said Bruce Claflin, vice president and general manager 
of Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  "With the unparal-
leled partnership we have with Microsoft, our dual architecture 
Intel-to-Alpha strategy, enterprise software enhancements, and a 
full range of worldwide integration and support services -- we have 
a significant lead over other computer vendors who have only begun 
to initiate their Windows NT-based programs and solutions."

     "It's our breadth of experience in providing enterprise-wide 
solutions that makes us the leading provider of Windows NT-based 
solutions in the market today," said Lucia Quinn, vice president of 
strategic marketing and brand management in Digital's Personal 
Computer Business Unit.  "We were the first enterprise computer 
company to commit to the Windows NT-based market, working closely 
with customers for more than four years.  They've told us what they
need for success in their enterprise environments and that is 
clearly reflected in today's announcements:  We do it right, we do 
it best and we did it first -- no other vendor of Windows NT-based 
solutions can make that claim."

     "Enterprise users will be the ones to ultimately benefit from 
Digital's extensive array of platforms and solutions for 
Microsoft(R) Windows(R) and Windows NT," said Rich Tong, vice 
president of marketing and training, desktop and business systems 
division at Microsoft Corp.  "The combination of Digital's wide 
range of high-performance Intel and Alpha platforms with the robust,
easy-to-use Microsoft Windows family of operating systems provides 
enterprise customers with a highly available, cost-effective and 
manageable computing solution."

Bringing the Enterprise to the Desktop

     In keeping with the company's goal to be a leader in supplying
Windows-based solutions across the enterprise -- and an undisputed 
world leader in delivering Windows NT-based products and support -- 
Digital today introduced an expansion to its value line of Venturis 
desktops and a complete new line of its Celebris family of 
"enterprise-ready" clients.  As a result, Digital now delivers the 
most formidable Pentium Pro, Windows NT-optimized line-up in the
industry.

Venturis  GL -- The Leading Value Line for General Business Users

     The new Venturis GL joins the recently introduced and highly 
affordable Venturis FX family to deliver to mainstream business 
users price-value-performance and integrated technology targeted for 
deployment across the commercial environment.  As with all Digital 
PCs, Digital ClientWORKS is included with the new systems, giving 
customers increased manageability and reducing total cost of 
ownership.  The Venturis GL is available with Pentium Pro 180- and 
200-megahertz (MHz) microprocessors and is optimized for Windows NT 
4.0 Workstation.  Available immediately worldwide, estimated street 
prices for the Venturis GL begin at U.S. $2,299.  

Celebris FX and Celebris GL -- "Enterprise-Ready" Clients

     Digital's new Celebris family is a premium line of 
"enterprise-ready" clients that make it easier to install, configure 
and manage desktops within the enterprise.  Each system includes 
Digital's ClientWORKS management software, Digital's cluster-ready 
software for high data availability and Windows NT 4.0 Workstation 
pre-configured across the line.

     The Celebris FX family includes models with Pentium 133, 166 
and 200MHz microprocessors, integrated 10BaseT/2 networking and 
comes pre-loaded with Windows NT and Windows 95 -- allowing users to 
choose the 32-bit operating system that best meets their needs.  The 
systems are available immediately worldwide with estimated street 
prices starting at U.S. $1,749.  

     The Celebris GL, Digital's high-performance enterprise client, 
includes models based on 180 and 200MHz Pentium Pro microprocessors 
and features integrated Matrox graphics, built-in audio and support 
for Universal Serial Bus.  The system also comes integrated with a 
10BaseT/2 network interface and is upgradeable to 100BaseTX with a 
daughter card, saving an expansion slot. Available immediately 
worldwide, estimated street prices for the Celebris GL begin at U.S. 
$2,609.  

The Leader in Mobile Computing for the Enterprise

     Reinforcing its position as a leader in bringing Windows 
NT-based computing to the mobile environment, Digital today 
announced the industry's only fully integrated Windows NT 4.0-based 
solution for notebook computing.  The award-winning HiNote Ultra II, 
the thinnest and lightest Pentium notebook computer on the market, 
is available with Windows NT 4.0 Workstation pre-loaded and pre-
configured with power management and plug-and-play-like features --
making Windows NT-based mobile computing a practical reality for the 
first time.

     The HiNote Ultra II models for Windows NT 4.0 Workstation 
include exclusive advancements developed to deliver unprecedented 
Windows NT performance on a notebook computer.  These include 
hot-docking support for the system's broad range of expansion 
options -- such as the HiNote Ultra Mobile Media Module with 
6X-speed CD-ROM drive or the system's port-replicator option -- as 
well as hot insertion and removal of a variety of popular PC Card 
peripherals, such as Digital's Roam About wireless network card.

     Digital-designed power management features not only deliver 
extended battery life under Windows NT 4.0, but also provide similar 
battery life and power management to Windows 95.  Additional 
usability improvements of Digital's mobile implementation under 
Windows NT 4.0 include a battery gauge for monitoring system 
run-time between charges.  Available in the U.S. later this month, 
estimated street prices for the HiNote Ultra II with Windows NT 4.0 
Workstation begin at U.S. $4,999.  

Windows NT Enterprise Servers Designed from the Ground Up

     Digital's Prioris and AlphaServers -- with record-breaking 
database performance -- are optimized to deliver more scaleability 
through symmetrical multiprocessing across Intel and Alpha 
platforms; more manageability through Digital's ServerWORKS, 
ClientWORKS and POLYCENTER enterprise management software tools; and 
more availability through advanced hardware features and Digital 
Clusters for Windows NT Server software.  Several new enhancements 
across Digital's full line of server solutions -- including the 
recently announced 400MHz AlphaServer 4000 family -- yield 
additional benefits in scaleability, manageability and availability 
for the Windows enterprise.

     With the newest version of ServerWORKS Manager -- Digital's 
intuitive, standards-based server and network manageability software 
that ships standard with every Digital Windows NT server -- Digital 
delivers the most manageable server solutions on the market 
optimized for Windows NT 4.0.  Available immediately worldwide, new 
features of ServerWORKS Manager version 2.0 include remote paging, 
management of Windows NT clustered servers, an intelligent toolbar 
and full integration with Digital's DMI-based ClientWORKS management 
software.  

     Also optimized for Windows NT 4.0 is the latest version of 
Digital Clusters for Windows NT Server -- software that provides 
high availability with user-transparent, automatic failover between 
two Digital servers.  New features of Digital Clusters for Windows 
NT Server version 1.0a include real-time failover monitoring, 
notification and recovery management through Digital's ServerWORKS 
Manager and faster installation through Digital's ServerWORKS Quick 
Launch configuration utility.

     Digital also announced today an all-in-one kit for support of 
Digital Clusters for Windows NT Server 1.0a.  The Prioris Server 
Cluster Kit enables resellers to easily build a pair of clustered 
servers for high availability in networked applications based on 
Windows NT 4.0, with failover support for Windows NT File Services, 
Microsoft SQL Server 6.5, and Oracle Workgroup Server.  Estimated 
street pricing for the Prioris Server Cluster Kit is U.S. $3,000.  

     With broad operating systems and LAN device support, tight 
integration with mobile or desktop clients via ClientWORKS, and 
SNMP-based integration for enterprise network managers such as 
POLYCENTER NetView on Windows NT, Digital's server solutions also 
provide the lowest cost of ownership for enterprise LAN managers.

Digital to Extend Personal Workstations Lead

     Continuing its leadership position in providing Windows 
NT-based enterprise solutions, Digital is readying its next-
generation family of high-performance Windows NT-based personal 
workstations.  The new personal workstations will be announced later 
this quarter and will be based on Intel's Pentium Pro micro-processor.  
The new offerings will fuel the growing volume market for Windows 
NT-based workstations and will boost Digital's lead in driving the 
market for Windows NT-based solutions in corporate and technical 
computing environments.

     Digital's solutions are the leading choice for customers 
deploying Windows NT across the enterprise.  The company offers 
enterprise customers superior value with client/server solutions 
optimized for Windows and Windows NT environments, global services 
and support, and solutions delivered through alliances with industry 
leaders.

     For on-line product photos and more information on Digital 
please visit www.newsdesk.com

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
