           Digital Launches Second-Generation Colorwriter
                      LSR 2000+ Laser Printers


       Colorwriter LSR 2000+ Models Offer Leading Performance
                     and Features at Lower Cost


MAYNARD, Mass., September 11, 1996 -- Broadening its coverage into 
the office network color market, Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced its family of second-generation high-performance color 
laser printers, the Colorwriter LSR 2000+. The family consists of 
two models, a powerful but attractively priced entry-level model, 
and a premium priced, high-performance model, targeted to 
production-quality printing. The high-performance model adds a 20% 
performance increase over the current Colorwriter model, and 
includes support for Windows 95, Windows NT and Macintosh. Both 
models include an upgraded one-year on-site warranty. 

     "Color laser printing is a growing segment of our product 
line," said Rob Hannemann, general manager, Printing Business 
Systems, "and these color laser printers offer an unbeatable value 
at two important price points, with the high-performance, quality of 
output, and advanced features for today's evolving color printing 
requirements."

     The Colorwriter LSR 2000+ provides fast network printing of 
near-photographic quality color output. Powered by an EFI Fiery XJe 
Controller, it prints up to 3 pages per minute (ppm) in color and 12 
ppm in monochrome. Its eight-bit color depth, full continuous tone 
output of 600 dot-per-inch (dpi) resolution is comparable to high-
end color laser copiers and printers, effectively filling the gap 
between low-end desktop color lasers and high-end color laser 
copiers.

     The Colorwriter LSR 2000+ offers processing performance up to 
six times faster than that of other leading desktop color lasers, 
with a quality of output a fraction of the cost of color laser 
copiers. Other features include:

     *	RIP-While-Print functionality, allowing images to be 
        processed while other images are being printed

     *	Memory compression, eliminating unnecessary RAM costs

     *	Continuous print capability, assuring operation at 
        maximum-rated speed

     *	Adobe PostScript Level 2, guaranteeing compatibility with 
        the industry standard

     *	Connectivity for mixed platform Macintosh, PC, UNIX 
        workgroup environments through built-in Centronics Parallel 
        and Ethernet ports

     *	Local languages for utilities, documentation and front panel 
        displays

     *	Energy Star compliance

     *	One year on-site warranty


     The entry-level model, which comes with 16 MB of upgradeable 
memory, is designed for high-quality office color printing for such 
applications as desktop publishing, overhead transparencies, and 
proposals.  The second model comes with 32 MB of memory and the Professional 
Color Kit, consisting of the LSR manager, downloader, spooler and 
print calibrator utilities--all newly designed for Windows 95, 
Windows NT and Macintosh. This model is a high-performance solution 
for graphics, pre-press and digital publishing.

     The Colorwriter LSR 2000+ is available now through Digital-
authorized resellers and distributors. The 16 MB model is list 
priced at $9,499.  The 32 MB model is list priced at $10,699.

