                            Digital Extends Portfolio
                         for Internet Business Computing
                          
              
           Major Solutions Target High-Growth Internet Market Segments


MAYNARD, Mass. -- September 16, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
extended its vast portfolio of Internet offerings with major new products 
and services to solve customers' business-critical requirements for 
Internet computing.  Included in the new lineup of hardware, software, 
networking, and services are:

     *	"Internet-Energized" AlphaServer systems -- bundled with full Internet 
     	functionality at no extra cost -- for UNIX(R), Microsoft(R) Windows 
        NT(R), and OpenVMS platforms.

     *	Licensing and planned incorporation in Digital UNIX and OpenVMS 64-bit 
     	operating systems of Java technology from Sun Microsystems, Inc.

     *	New Internet and intranet services -- Intranet Planning and 
        Organization, AltaVista Search Consulting, Internet AltaVista Tunneling, 
        and Digital Information Center/Distance Learning -- to help customers 
        plan and organize an intranet; identify their information retrieval 
        requirements and access internal data; build secure virtual networks; 
        and train employees, regardless of their location.

     *	Networking products -- RouteAbout Access ES and DECNIS Version 4.0 
     	software -- that helps businesses connect remotely to the Internet and 
        set up corporate intranets.

     "Digital is providing complete, industrial-strength Internet solutions 
for three high-growth market segments:  Internet service providers (ISPs), 
corporate intranets, and Internet commerce,"  said Rose Ann Giordano, vice 
president of the Internet Business Group.  "As the Internet explosion 
drives the use of public networks for business use, Digital's products, 
services, alliances and partnerships will take our customers into the 
next-generation Internet."  Giordano will deliver a keynote address at 
Networld + Interop entitled, "The Next-Generation Internet,"  at 9 AM 
Thursday, Sept. 19, at the Georgia World Congress Center in Atlanta, GA.
Internet-Energized AlphaServer Systems

     "Today we are announcing an industry-first,"  said Pauline Nist, vice 
president of the AlphaServer Business Segment.  "Every AlphaServer system 
we ship, on every operating system Digital supports, is now 'Internet-energized' 
with the critical applications customers need to quickly and easily set up Web 
sites.  This unique, no-cost offering, coupled with AlphaServer systems, the 
world's fastest-growing business computing platform, provides an unbeatable 
Internet and intranet solution." 

     Digital is the only computer company to deliver full Internet 
functionality across all of its operating systems, offering unparalleled 
performance, choice and flexibility.  For the highest availability and 
investment protection, Digital also provides mix-or-match failover 
capabilities for all Internet-energized AlphaServer Systems.

     Every Digital UNIX AlphaServer system now ships with an Apache web server 
and a library of Internet shareware, such as mail and news groups. The 
64-bit Digital UNIX, unmatched in scaling, enables simultaneous support 
of more than 2,000 remote and 4,000 TCP/IP connections.

     All Microsoft Windows NT systems from Digital now ship with the Internet 
Roadmap for Windows NT Version 2.  It includes important Internet-enabling 
software in both shareware and evaluation versions.  As part of the 
Microsoft/Digital Alliance for Enterprise Computing, Digital further benefits 
customers by supporting a full range of consulting, security, training, systems 
integration, and support services for Microsoft's Internet Server Solutions.

     The OpenVMS Internet Product Suite provides Internet functionality to 
the half-million OpenVMS systems deployed worldwide.   OpenVMS provides 
64-bit virtual addressing, new threading capabilities, and a revolutionary 
file system, enabling users to manage much larger volumes of data while 
maintaining continuous system availability.

     AlphaServer systems hold the world record for Internet performance in the 
industry-standard SPECweb96 benchmark.  In addition, BYTE magazine recently 
named the AlphaServer 1000 "Editors Choice" Internet server in 
head-to-head competition with Apple, Intergraph, SGI, Sun, and other Web 
servers.

New Support for Sun Microsystems, Inc.'s Java on Alpha                          

      Digital is now licensing the Java technology from Sun Microsystems, 
Inc., and will make it available with the Digital UNIX and OpenVMS 64 bit 
operating systems.  Because Java will be incorporated in these operating 
systems, the Java Virtual Machine(R) will be transparently available to users, 
who will no longer need to download it in application software.  Digital's 
licensing of Java also enables Digital UNIX and OpenVMS users to take advantage 
of the high-performance 64-bit Alpha environment to boost Java performance. 
Digital's Just-in-Time (JIT) compiler leverages Alpha to achieve tremendous 
speed executing platform-independent Java applets and applications.

    Java is well-suited for the development of Internet applications and 
will play an important role in Digital's strategy to bring enterprise-strength 
Internet solutions to customers.  The Java Development kit will be available to  
Digital UNIX users by the end of 1996, and will be bundled with the next major 
release of Digital UNIX.  Java Run Time support for OpenVMS will begin to roll 
out in 1997.

Complete Intranet and Internet Services						

     The Digital Services Division is augmenting its portfolio of intranet and 
Internet services.  New offerings include:

     *	Intranet Planning and Organization, which uses a workshop format to 
     	transfer to customers the knowledge gained by Digital in implementing 
        its own intranet.

     *	AltaVista Search Consulting, which helps customers identify their 
     	information retrieval requirements and access internal data quickly and 
     	easily, using AltaVista indexing technology.

     *	Internet AltaVista Tunneling, a security evaluation and product 
     	installation service that enables customers to build virtual private 
     	networks with their customers, partners and suppliers, securely linking 
     	their virtual organizations.

     *	Digital Information Center/Distance Learning, a multimedia educational 
     	system with information authoring, user and system administration, and 
     	management reporting capabilities for groups that need to regularly 
        train employees regardless of their locations.

     Digital services will also include Microsoft "Normandy" integration 
expertise.  Normandy is an integrated family of scalable Internet/intranet 
server applications based on the Microsoft Windows NT Server network operating 
system.  It enhances users' Web and corporate intranet experiences by enabling 
them to interact in real time, locate other users, and find and share 
information, thereby creating virtual communities of interest.

     Digital is the first systems integrator to help customers implement 
Normandy.  Digital will provide beta customers services including network design 
and deployment, integration of Normandy with legacy systems, customer support 
and help desk, application development, and other consulting services.
Networking Products Provide Internet Foundation

     To maximize the potential of the servers and software announced today, 
Digital also is introducing two new networking products that help businesses tap 
the power of the Internet and to set up corporate intranets. 

       RouteAbout Access ES is a low-cost IP router ideal for small offices that 
need remote connections to a central site or the Internet.  As the newest 
member of Digital's RouteAbout family of access routers, it provides an 
Ethernet-to-WAN connection up to T1 speeds and can be used for leased lines and 
frame relay implementations.  The product is available now for $850.

     Also announced today are software and hardware enhancements to the DECNIS 
high-end router.  DECNIS Version 4.0 software offers the Secure Connection 
Firewall, which enables ISPs to set up secure network domains in multiprotocol 
(IP, DECnet and OSI) environments.  For ease of management, the new software 
also supports the clearVISN Router Configurator.   A new process controller for 
the DECNIS product provides increased performance, and a new management 
processor offers ISPs the faster convergences times required to support large 
networks.  Available in October, the new DECNIS process controller is priced at 
$3,000 for a 16 Mbyte system and $5,500 for a 32 Mbyte system.

     As part of Digital's enVISN network architecture, the new products work 
together with the recently announced high-performance VNswitch and GIGAswitch/IP 
products to offer customers and ISPs top performance and reliability.

     "The full range of products and services available from Digital and its 
partners makes us the only choice for companies seriously interested in 
using the Internet to increase profits, decrease costs, or gain a competitive 
advantage," said Giordano.  "Digital truly brings business computing to the 
Internet."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/server 
solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide information 
systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, storage, networking, 
software and services, together with industry-focused solutions from business 
partners, help organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.

     For more information about Digital and its partners, visit Digital's home 
page at http://www.digital.com
