                  Digital Equipment Corporation Meets Growing
       Demand For Intranets With Suite Of Services For Burgeoning Market


           ....Introduction of Four New Services Complements Existing
                Digital Internet/Intranet Services Portfolio...


MAYNARD, Massachusetts -- September 18, 1996 -- In response to specific 
needs identified by IT managers worldwide and the rapidly growing use of 
Intranet technologies in global business, Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced four new Internet/Intranet services:

     o	  Intranet Planning and Organization
     o	  AltaVista Search Consulting
     o	  Internet AltaVista Tunneling
     o	  Digital Information Center/Distance Learning
     	  
Internet Planning and Organization (IPO) Service

     The IPO Service is aimed to assist companies with the design, development,
guidelines and standards for corporate Intranets -- reducing the time-to-market
and cost often associated with the task.  Using a workshop format to transfer
the knowledge gained by Digital in implementing its own award-winning Intranet,
IPO addresses the multiple elements associated with creating and managing
Intranets, including business uses, architecture, organization, indexing and
searching, and standards and security. 

     The Digital Intranet has more than 90,000 TCP/IP nodes, about 1,100 
web servers and nearly one million Web pages.  The Digital Intranet 
recently won two Business On The Internet (BOTI) awards from Network Computing 
and CommunicationsWeek publications.  In winning two of the five Intranet 
awards, Digital was cited for the Most Comprehensive Intranet and the Best 
Leading Edge Intranet Technology.

     Customers may opt for the Basic IPO Service, a one-day seminar for 
those who have deployed partial Intranets and have fundamental technical 
knowledge, or the Complete IPO Service, a multiple-day workshop for those who 
are just beginning to plan for an Intranet and need guidance on many technical 
and operational subjects.  Follow-on consulting is also available to help 
develop a customized Intranet strategy, design, and plan.
AltaVista Tunnel Service

     The AltaVista Tunnel Service allows customers to connect onsite users 
with mobile workers, including sales people, telecommuters, suppliers, 
contractors and consumers to create customized Virtual Private Networks that 
enable users to securely share time-sensitive and confidential information.

     The services include an implementation plan, evaluation of security 
policies, and configuration and installation of AltaVista Tunnel.  A low cost
alternative to dedicated leased lines and long distance direct dial, the
AltaVista Tunnel Service enables more efficient and secure management of wide
area networks and mobile workers.  It is offered in both Personal (PC-based)
and Workshop (server-based) editions.

     Newcourt Credit Group in Canada has been using AltaVista Tunnel since last
March.  Following several days of consulting services, Newcourt Credit
immediately implemented Internet-based communications with its consumer and
business customers across North America.  The company eliminated modem pools
producing an immediate cost savings around support of the modems and toll
charges.  "In addition to the savings, we now have a more secure network,"
explains Sharon Regan, manager, systems, Newcourt Credit.  "With the Digital
Tunnel and Firewall products we're able to make maximum use of the Internet in
a controlled environment." 

AltaVista Search Consulting

     Based on Digital's award-winning AltaVista Search Intranet Private 
eXtension, the AltaVista Search Consulting Service is a workshop-based 
consulting service in which Digital experts assist users with the:

     o	 establishment of information retrieval requirements;
     o	 planning, design and implementation of AltaVista search products;
     o	 identification and protection of confidential information; and
     o	 customization and integration of indexed documents
     
     The AltaVista Search Consulting Service enables organizations to 
apply the searching and indexing technology of AltaVista Search Intranet 
Private eXtension to their Intranet Web pages.  And the user-friendly system 
enables quick and accurate access and retrieval of useful, business-critical
information.

Digital Information Center/Distance Learning

     The Digital Information Center/Distance Learning Service provides an
Internet style distance learning solution for organizations that regularly
train employees on new technologies, products, policies or services.  It offers
an integrated solution for the authoring and distribution of information, user
and system administration, and management reporting. 

     Leveraging state-of-the-art multimedia and courseware authoring 
tools, Digital employs standard Internet-browser technology to provide 
customized and interactive training sessions to employees anytime, at any 
location, at their own pace.

     This service not only streamlines communications and increases 
employee productivity, but results in significant cost reductions as well. 
Employees can take training when it is convenient for their work schedule and 
proceed at their own pace providing significant savings in travel, logistics, 
and lost productivity when compared to traditional classroom instruction.

     These four new services are in addition to Digital's Internet 
Services Roadmap introduced last October and the Internet Solution Set 
announced last February.  The entire Internet/Intranet products and services 
portfolio announced over the past 11 months is designed to meet a variety of 
customer requirements with flexible offerings.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/server
solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide information systems. 
Digital's scaleable Alpha and Intel platforms, storage, networking, software
and services, together with industry-focused solutions from business partners,
help organizations compete and win in todayis global marketplace. 

