                      Powerful AltaVista Search Technology
                   Extends Onsite Computing to Private Intranets


          ..searching for business information becomes as fast and easy
                      as searching on the Worldwide Web...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- September 18, 1996 -- In a bold move that demonstrates
the power of AltaVista's OnSite Computing vision, Digital Equipment
Corporation today announced the availability of AltaVista Search Intranet
Private eXtension (PX).  With this announcement, businesses can gain the
same the award-winning search capabilities of AltaVista extended from the
worldwide web to their private domain, making it fast and simple to find
valuable business information on company intranets.

     Shipping at the end of September, AltaVista Search Intranet PX operates
behind corporate firewalls to index and locate terabytes of data on company
web and file servers, dramatically increasing business users' productivity.
Authorized users can access AltaVista Search Intranet Private eXtension
from their desktops using any popular Web browser, including Microsoft's
Internet Explorer or Netscape's Navigator, V2.0 or higher.

      "As companies expand their use of Intranet technology to help them compete
in today's global business environment, instant access to information is
critical to achieving success," said Ilene H. Lang, vice president of
Digital's Internet Software Business Unit.  "With AltaVista Search Intranet
Private eXtension, we are making the most comprehensive Web search and
retrieval capabilities available to private domains -- allowing individuals
immediate access to the information they need, from anywhere at anytime."

     Using the same high performance super-spider technology as Digital's
AltaVista Search Public Service, the Intranet Private eXtension crawls all
of the Web servers throughout the enterprise.  Every word on the private
intranet is indexed and made available along with information from the
public Internet.   A listing of AltaVista search results is presented in
seconds, and each item in the listing is hyperlinked directly to the
referenced intranet or Internet source

     Future versions of AltaVista Search Intranet PX will support many popular
office applications, such as word processing documents, presentation files,
spreadsheets and email messages.  A Software Developers Kit will be
available in a later release to allow for indexing of proprietary document
formats, and an Application Programming Interface will be available in the
future for systems integration efforts.

System Requirements and Pricing

     AltaVista Search Intranet Private eXtension runs on 64-bit Digital
AlphaServers running Digital UNIX.  Two versions of the product are
available: one for very-large memory (VLM) applications -- terabytes of
indexed information and tens of thousands of users -- and one for non-VLM
applications.

     For VLM applications running on Digital AlphaServers with more than 2GB of
main memory, AltaVista Search Intranet PX is priced at $69,999.95,
including a 250 user license.  Additional 250-user licenses can be added at
a price of $5,999.95 each, or an unlimited use license can be added for
$34,000.00.

     For non-VLM applications running on Digital AlphaServers with 2GB or less
main memory,  AltaVista Search Intranet PX is priced at $15,999.95,
including a 250-user license.  Additional 250-user licenses can be added
for $5,999.95 each, or an unlimited user license can be added for
$34,000.00.

Availability

     AltaVista Search Intranet Private eXtension is available for download from
the AltaVista software World Wide Web site
(http://www.altavista.software.digital.com) and will also be available
through resellers, catalogue vendors, ISPs, VARs and Digital Equipment
Corporation.

     AltaVista OnSite software solutions from Digital provide high performance
Internet connectivity to help cyberworkers quickly find useful information,
easily communicate and collaborate over secure virtual networks.  Further
information is available at http://altavista.software.digital.com.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/server
solutions from personal computers to integrated worldwide information
systems.  Digital's scaleable Alpha and Intel platforms, together with
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help organizations
compete and win in today's global marketplace.
