                Cobb County School District Awards Digital $6.5M
                          Network Deployment Contract
 

             ...Internet Access, Email, and Multimedia Applications 
                             Available Next Year...


MARIETTA, Georgia -- September 18, 1996 -- The Cobb County School 
District today announced that its high capacity, high performance network 
is scheduled to be completed in early 1997.  To launch this major technology
initiative, the Cobb County School District has chosen Digital Equipment
Corporation to lead the planning, design, and implementation of the school-wide 
network.  The local and wide area network will connect 91 schools and 
administrative offices in the county located outside of Atlanta.

     The $6.5M award, approved last May, follows an earlier $490,000 contract
with Digital to plan and design the school system's entry on the Information
Superhighway.  As the prime contractor for the Cobb Educational Network (Cobb
EduNet), Digital is overseeing all aspects of the project from wiring and
installation of computer and network systems to a firewall to protect all
schools and offices from unauthorized access.  With more than 85,000 students
in kindergarten through 12th grade, the Cobb County School District is the
third largest in Georgia and 35th largest in the United States. 

     The wiring of the buildings for networked computing and Internet access in
each classroom began two months ago and computer labs are being installed in
more than 120 rooms.  When the Cobb EduNet is complete next year, there will be
3,000 new personal computers and 500 new Apple Macintoshes for a wide range of
applications such as email, Internet access, word processing, graphics, school
administration, and purchasing.  "Digital has proven that its experience in
networking and the Internet is a good match for us as we move to the forefront
in the use of technology in the schools," said Jerry Ingram, superintendent,
Cobb County School District.  "Students will be able to use the Internet to
communicate and perform research and work collaboratively between schools and
with other Internet sites across the globe. Every school will be able to
provide a wealth of information to the rest of the world." 

     "This project takes advantage of Digital's strengths in planning and 
building a complex, multivendor network," explains Graeme Shorter, vice 
president, Enterprise Networks and Platform Technologies.  "The complexity and 
cost of technology requires that an experienced integrator provide solutions 
to meet today's needs, but with the flexibility to cost effectively grow the 
network as requirements change."						

     The Cobb EduNet encompasses a variety of hardware, software, 
networking equipment, and services including the following:

     o	 Digital AlphaServer systems

     o	 Digital firewall services						

     o	 Cisco 7500 and 2500 series routers					

     o	 3Com switches and hubs							

     o	 AMP Copper and fiber cabling						

     o	 BellSouth frame relay services						

     o	 Dell, IBM, Compaq, Apple PCs and servers				

     o	 Microsoft Windows 95, Works, and Office				

     o	 Novell NetWare 4.1							

     o	 Adtran CSU/DSU equipment


     The Cobb County School District includes 91 schools (95 by 1998) and 
various central and administrative office locations.  The mission of the 
school system is to guarantee a quality educational program for all students in
a challenging environment.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/server
solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide information 
systems.

      Digital's Alpha and Intel platforms, storage, networking, software 
and services, together with industry-focused solutions from business 
partners, help organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.

