               Digital Demonstrates Breadth of Internet Solutions
                                at Networld+Interop


		     Networking Booth 3942, Hall D
		     Microsoft/Digital Alliance Booth 6132, Hall G
		     Semiconductor Booth 6426, Hall G


ATLANTA, September 18, 1996 -- At the Networld+Interop exhibition here
this week, Digital Equipment Corporation is showing businesses how its
networked computing solutions and Internet expertise can help them
meet today's complex challenges.  Highlights of the show include Rose
Ann Giordano's keynote address on "Accessing the Next Generation
Internet", demonstrations of IP Switching solutions and participation
of Digital's AltaVista Search Service in the "Web Search Engine Challenge."

     To cover the full range of its networked offerings, Digital is hosting
three booths and participating in several multivendor showcases
throughout the exhibition. 

     Rose Ann Giordano, vice president of Digital's Internet Business
Group, will deliver Thursday morning's keynote address on "Accessing the Next 
Generation Internet."  The session will offer insights into the future of the 
Internet, focusing on how the evolution of the Internet over the next generation 
will drive models from early technology-driven sites to business-driven
sites to tomorrow's society-driven sites.  Giordano will introduce the concept 
of the Internet Helix, which highlights the inner relationship of technology, 
business and societal dynamics driving the Internet's growth.  The session will 
be held from 9:00 - 10:00 in the Jack Murphy Ball Room at the Georgia World
Congress Center. 

Network Infrastructure Takes Shape in Networking Booth 

     Demonstrations in Digital's Networking booth, #3942 in Hall D,
show how Digital's flexible networking solutions can help enterprises and 
Internet Service Providers transition smoothly to today's high-performance 
intranet and Internet solutions.  From the recently announced VNswitch 900 
multi-technology switches to secure access products and clearVISN policy-based 
network management, Digital's enVISN network architecture offers
customers complete, cost-effective solutions.  Experts are also available to 
discuss how Digital's Network and Systems Integration Services group can provide 
world-class multivendor solutions and support.

     Attendees interested in how IP Switching can address their bandwidth
needs today can see demonstrations of Digital's GIGAswitch/IP Solution
in the networking booth, #3942 in Hall D.  Experts will be available
to compare the benefits of this current solution, which today supports
both IP switching and ATM Forum LAN emulation, with future schemes proposed by 
other vendors.  Digital is also participating in the IP Switching Showcase, 
Booth 762 in Hall A, where many vendors will demonstrate the broad range of IP 
Switching solutions available to take advantage of this powerful new product 
category. 

     Digital experts will also be available to discuss the emerging
market for Gigabit Ethernet solutions in the Gigabit Ethernet Alliance booth, 
Booth 5860 in Hall F.                                                         

New Windows NT Products Featured in Microsoft/Digital Alliance Booth

     At the Microsoft/Digital Alliance booth -- #6132 -- attendees can see
the newest products resulting from the Microsoft/Digital Alliance for
Enterprise Computing.  The new products, including the Venturis GL Desktop PCs, 
Celebris FX and Celebris GL Desktop PCs, and HiNote Ultra II with Windows NT 
4.0, secure Digital as the logical choice for Windows NT products across the 
enterprise.  Now in its second year, the Alliance combines both companies' 
strengths and resources to solve complex customer problems, helping customers 
develop, deploy, manage, migrate and integrate Windows-based solutions more 
quickly, completely and cost-effectively than any other vendor. 
Cardbus Offerings Featured in Semiconductor Booth

     In Booth 6426, Digital Semiconductor is promoting the advantages of 
10/100Mbps (megabits per second) Ethernet communications for Cardbus, as 
well as low-cost network solutions for both desktop and laptop PCs.  A 
graphical, "bridge-building" demonstration shows the superior network 
performance of the 21143 PCI-Cardbus Fast Ethernet controller chip for 
mobile computers.  Nearby, a videoconference demonstration links systems 
using 10/100Mbps 21140A PCI Fast Ethernet chips.  Fast screen refresh rates made 
possible by the 100Mbps, full-duplex solution illustrate its clear advantage 
over traditional 10Mbps Ethernet in real-world applications.

     Digital Semiconductor is also conducting its semiannual drawing for a 
free, network-ready PC, open to all Networld+Interop attendees.  Details 
for participation can be obtained in Booth 6426.

AltaVista Search Service Competes for Honors

     Digital's AltaVista Search Service will be participating in PC Computing's
"Web Search Engine Challenge" to test the speed and accuracy of today's top 
search engines.  Digital will participate in the Challenges at 11:00 a.m. 
Wednesday, September 18 and Thursday, September 19.  The shootouts will take 
place in the PC Computing booth (925H) in the Interop DotCom pavilion.  In 
addition, AltaVista software solutions for OnSite Computing will be on display 
in the Digital booth.  OnSite Computing solutions provide direct access to 
information and people simply and quickly, and uses standard Web browsers to 
bring the universal Internet to a company's intranet.

