Network and Systems Integration Services, a business unit of Digital's 
Services Division, is dedicated to helping customers successfully 
apply information technology to achieve significant improvement in 
their business performance.  It was formed in July 1996 through the 
merger of two existing organizations, Network Services and Systems 
Integration.  Technical and program management expertise in networks, 
systems, and applications disciplines offers customers a single point 
of contact for many of their requirements.

     Network and Systems Integration is part of the $6.2B Services Division 
at Digital.  The other business units: Multivendor Customer Services 
and Operations Management Services, together with Network and Systems 
Integration deliver a broad range of support, maintenance, and 
consulting services across varied computing and networked business 
computing environments in approximately 100 countries.

     Network and Systems Integration recognizes the increasing importance 
of networked computing where systems and applications converge in 
complex, multivendor environments.  The organization_s focus is on 
connectivity within and between enterprises and information resources 
including:

     *	    Providing full platform and applications migration services around 
     	    Microsoft Windows NT

     *	    Planning, designing, and implementing Intra/Internet-based mail and 
     	    network technologies

     *	    Planning, designing, implementing, and managing the technology 
     	    required for Internet-based electronic commerce

     *	    Delivering high performance computing/VLDB (very large database) 
     	    experience for data mining and data warehouse
     	    
     With 6,200 employees worldwide, the business unit primarily serves 
medium to large enterprises.  Among the skills are the following:


     *	    700 Windows NT certified professionals

     *	    500 network solution architects

     *	    1,300 applications consultants and developers

     *	    500 mail/messaging and EDI experts

     The implementation of multivendor, mission critical customer solutions 
draws heavily on Networks and Systems Integration's core competencies 
of designing, building, and integrating network-based applications, 
utilizing capabilities in such key areas as solutions architecture, 
project management, and vertical industry expertise.  Industries 
served range from financial institutions to communications, 
manufacturing, and the public sector.

     In conjunction with Coopers and Lybrand, the organization developed 
the Digital Program Methodology (DPM) in use at more than 1,200 
projects worldwide.  It is a structured approach to managing customer 
programs and projects.  DPM provides consistent processes for 
planning deliverables, managing change, assuring quality, and handling 
training activities.  The methodology is regularly updated based on 
field experience and competitive analysis.  Knowledge transfer to 
customers is a key component of the services delivered.

     By investing in the development of consistent processes and management 
across geographies, the group has specialized knowledge of 
industry-specific needs.  Industry solution sets include:

     *	    TeMIP: Network and service management platform for 
     	    telecommunications industries

     *	    BASEstar: Manufacturing industry integration framework for 
            real-time factory floor management

     *	    PDAS: Process Data Acquisition Services, a certified extension to 
     	    SAP_s core application used in process manufacturing industries

     *	    DEC/EDI:  Software and services that link customers' enterprises 
     	    with supply chain partners

     Network and Systems Integration serves customers through its own 
dedicated sales force and account managers from other Digital 
businesses.  To address customer preferences to buy services from 
different sources, Network and Systems Integration has established a 
number of alliances.  The most strategic partnership is with Microsoft 
covering mail/messaging, Intra/Internet, and applications development 
and deployment.  Other significant relationships exist with Andersen 
Consulting, Cisco Systems, Netscape, Oracle, and SAP .  Of course, 
Network and Systems Integration maintains close affiliations with 
various Digital product groups including Network Products, Alpha 
