              StorageWorks Now Available for Digital's
                         Windows NT Clusters


         ...RAID Storage to Windows NT Clusters Made Easy...


MAYNARD, Mass., September 23, 1996 --  Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced StorageWorks Windows NT Clusters Kits, giving users 
the benefits of high availability storage in NT cluster 
configurations.  Customers now can implement clusters easily for 
Windows NT on top of RAID configurations. 

     Today's announcement reinforces Digital's StorageWorks family 
as the industry's leading multiplatform storage solution, and 
further establishes Digital as the logical choice for customers 
requiring Windows NT as part of their enterprise computing 
environments. 

     The StorageWorks NT Cluster Kits, available now for Digital's 
AlphaServer and Intel-based Prioris servers, provide a high level of 
pre-configuration and integration that is not available from any 
other vendor in the NT cluster market today. The result is easier 
and faster cluster installation, including RAID storage for improved 
high availability in today's PC client/server LAN environment. 

     "The Windows NT marketplace is extremely hungry for high-
performance NT storage solutions," said William Storey, president of 
WSB technologies, a Windows NT software consulting company.  "The 
combination of Digital clusters for Windows NT software, running on 
AlphaServer and Prioris servers with StorageWorks products, provides 
a high availability solution today for Windows NT customers.  And 
it's a very cost effective solution as well." 

     Two cluster platform kits and one cluster enabling kit make it 
easy to configure high availability into NT cluster configurations 
for the StorageWorks RAID Array 310 and RAID Array 410 subsystems. 
For the first time, customers can purchase all components required 
for implementing Windows NT clusters on top of RAID configurations 
through a single part number. 

     The RAID Array 310 offers a low-cost, standalone RAID subsystem 
solution to users in medium-sized departments or large workgroups. 
Standard features include redundant hot-swappable power and cooling, 
read and write-back cache, and support for 10-60GB of storage 
capacity.  The RAID 410 offers comprehensive support for 
client/server and mission critical applications for small data 
centers or large departmental environments. Features include dual 
redundant controllers, read and write-back cache, redundant power 
cooling, and support for up to 100GB of storage. 

     "StorageWorks provides the storage infrastructure to maximize 
Windows NT cluster investments, which is what our customers really 
care about," said Diana Eastty, StorageWorks product marketing 
manager at Digital.  "These new packaged, solutions-oriented 
platform kits for Digital's Windows NT clusters ensure that the 
addition of RAID storage is easy and complete." 

     StorageWorks NT Cluster Kits are designed to support mission 
critical applications in production environments, which demand high 
availability, high performance and high reliability. 

Customer Applications 

     Customers running Windows NT applications that see data and 
application availability as critical to the success of their 
business can now rely on Digital's coupling of clustering and RAID 
technologies. Examples include: 

     o	Businesses that have delayed the deployment of 
        business-critical applications on Windows NT until RAID 
        storage subsystems are supported 

     o	Organizations that are making a strategic commitment to 
        Windows NT 

     o	PC LAN computing environments that require high availability 
        

     Business critical applications running on Windows NT demand 
clustering capabilities, which Digital supports today. Digital will 
continue to develop and deliver clustering technology in conjunction 
with Microsoft's clustering product when it becomes commercially 
available.  Now in its second year, The Microsoft/Digital Alliance 
for Enterprise computing represents extraordinary cooperation 
between the two companies to deliver technology, products, sales, 
service, and support. Under the Alliance, Microsoft and Digital 
cross-license patent portfolios and are bringing to market Windows 
NT clustering solutions. 

Pricing and Availability					    

     StorageWorks NT Cluster Kits are available immediately and 
range in price from $499 to $3,479.  For more information about 
Digital's complete line of storage hardware and software products, 
call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967) or visit 
http://www.storage.digital.com on the World Wide Web.

