		New Cash Dispenser Delivers Cash Faster


STOCKHOLM, Sweden, September 27, 1996 -- Digital Equipment has  
released a new model of its successful cash dispenser - FBS QUICK 
CASH. The new model delivers cash in less than 15 seconds at a 
minimum cost to the bank. It can be installed in any kind of 
semi-protected environment such as shopping malls, hotel receptions 
or railway stations.

Cash will be the major payment method for many years to come. 
Customers demand quick and easy access to cash, while banks need to 
minimize costs. Efficient, dedicated cash dispensers offer the best 
solution cheaper and faster than a full-function ATM.

The QUICK CASH has a new design, based on field-tested modules from 
earlier versions. It is extremely easy to use and install. It also 
offers the smallest footprint on the market. It supports both 
magnetic and smart cards and guides the users on either a colour or 
a monochrome screen. Receipt printing is optional.

Digital's QUICK CASH is ADA compliant and can be connected to 
Diebold 911/912 standards, Interbold I-series and NCR/NDC+ 
standards. Further, it supports a multitude of line protocols. It 
can also be delivered in a variety of configurations and in any 
colour the financial institution requests to support market branding 
and image.  

Even before its official release, QUICK CASH was already a success. 
The first order, for 400 units, came from Asia and will be delivered 
in October 1996.

The new Cash Dispenser belongs to the FBS (Financial Business 
System) family of Self ServicePoints, developed and manufactured by 
Digital's international competence center for Banking Automation, 
Digital BCFI.

Digital BCFI is Digital Equipment's worldwide solutions company for 
developing and marketing Automation Solutions for Delivery Systems 
in the Retail Financial Services Industry. It is located in Jdrfdlla 
outside Stockholm, Sweden. Digital BCFI was approved for ISO 9001 
certificate in 1995.
