               Digital Equipment Corporation Launches
                        'Decision Driver DM'
           Service to Provide Complete Data Mart Solution


    ... Allows customers to implement subject-specific data mart
        in less than six weeks vs. traditional 12 months ...
 

MAYNARD, MASS., Sept. 25, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today introduced Decision Driver DM, a comprehensive service package 
which includes software licenses and systems integration services to 
provide customers with a complete solution for designing and 
deploying data marts running on Windows NT Server-based platforms.  
Digital has joined with Business Objects, Informatica Corp., and 
Microsoft to provide all the software and consulting services needed 
to design, install, test, and manage this total data mart solution.  
Decision Driver DM is the first complete service in the industry 
focused on delivering a data warehousing solution based on Microsoft 
SQL Server.

     Data marts are highly-focused, line-of-business data warehouses 
geared to companies who are looking to rapidly implement a 
cost-effective means of providing information to users.  Decision 
Driver DM enables customers to implement a subject-specific data 
mart that will take advantage of the user's existing data to solve a 
business problem.  Customers can quickly experience and evaluate the 
business benefits of the latest technologies and methodologies 
without the long term project approach traditionally used.  
Digital's Decision Driver DM service, which can be deployed on 
either Alpha- or Intel-based servers, allows customers to design, 
test, and implement a complete data mart solution in less than six 
weeks for approximately $99,500, plus the cost of the server. 

Decision Driver DM includes the following components:

     -	Decision Support Tools:  BusinessObjects, a leading 
        integrated query, reporting, and OLAP tool that gives 
        non-technical end users the ability to access and analyze 
        data stored in data warehouses and data marts; 

     -	Extraction/Transformation Tools:  Informatica PowerMart 
        suite, an integrated set of client/server tools that address 
        all the major steps of data mart design and management, 
        including data extraction, mapping and transformation;

     - 	Database Engine:  Microsoft SQL Server, a scalable 
        high-performance relational database management system which 
        is easy to implement, offers superior price/performance, and 
        a complete infrastructure solution through its tight 
        integration with the Microsoft BackOffice family and other 
        Microsoft products and technologies;
  
     -	Implementation Assistance:  Up to six weeks of Digital 
        systems integration services, providing hands-on expertise 
        in the areas of data mart architecture and design, 
        implementation, training and support.

     "Digital has earned a leadership position in the data warehouse 
market over the past year," said Kannankote Srikanth, vice president 
of Digital's Network and Systems Integration business.  "Decision 
Driver DM service is an integral component of Digital's 
comprehensive data warehouse solutions portfolio.  It enables users 
to take advantage of their data to make timely, cost effective, and 
well-founded business decisions.  Teaming with best-in-class 
companies such as Business Objects, Informatica, and Microsoft 
allows us to further simplify our customers' business practices and 
enhance their organizational productivity."   

     Data marts have become one of the fastest growing segments of 
the data warehousing industry.  META Group, an analyst firm in 
Stamford, Conn., has estimated that the overall market for data 
warehousing should reach $13 billion by 1998.  According to a study 
conducted by International Data Corporation (IDC), companies in 
North America and Europe that have invested in decision support 
systems such as data marts have realized an average 401% ROI over a 
three year period.

     Commenting on this important joint initiative with Digital, 
Bernard Liautaud, president and CEO of Business Objects said, "The 
bundling of these complementary technologies provides customers with 
a solid data mart solution.  Business Objects' integrated query, 
reporting, and OLAP solution brings an intuitive end user tool to 
Digital's integrated packaged data mart, enabling customers to 
easily navigate in and analyze the wealth of information stored."

     "We are excited to work with Digital to help our mutual 
customers rapidly build and manage enterprise-scalable data marts," 
said Informatica CEO, Gaurav Dhillon.  "The Decision Driver DM 
service will bring Informatica's PowerMart suite to a new group of 
customers who will now be able to address critical business problems 
at the departmental level, without the high risks and complexity 
normally associated with traditional data warehousing."

     Decision Driver DM represents the first customer available 
example of a solution that ties into Microsoft's recently announced 
(September 17, 1996) data warehousing strategy.  The strategy 
focuses on making it easier for customers and independent software 
vendors (ISVs) to implement data warehousing solutions in a timely 
and cost-effective manner with Microsoft SQL Server.  

     "We are very pleased to be working closely with Digital under 
the umbrella of Microsoft and Digital's Alliance for Enterprise 
Computing," said Jim Ewel, group product manager for Microsoft SQL 
Server at Microsoft.  "The Decision Driver DM service and Microsoft 
SQL Server make it easier for customers to realize the benefits of 
data warehousing, with quicker implementation times and for less 
money compared to competing solutions."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is a world leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha and Intel platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
